-- emotion_mappings — the full emotional-search vocabulary, exported from
-- production on 9 October 2026 (Supabase project uzmvcgewxgvnybdhvsyx).
--
-- WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Until now the production database was the only copy of
-- this table: the original seed (spiritpedia-emotion-mappings.sql, ~3,488 rows)
-- was never committed, and 0011_emotion_vocabulary.sql holds only the 43 rows
-- added by hand on 7 Oct 2026. This file is every row — those 43 included.
--
-- DATA ONLY. The table itself is created by
-- supabase/migrations/0000_production_baseline.sql; run that first.
--
-- Exported read-only through the service-role API, ordered by emotion then
-- subject so a re-export diffs cleanly. id and created_at are kept, so a
-- rebuilt table is an exact copy. ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on the
-- (emotion, subject_slug) unique key makes the file safe to re-run, including
-- against production, where it changes nothing.
--
-- Split into statements of 250 rows: one statement of this size has been
-- truncated in the Supabase SQL editor before (see 0011), so a partial paste
-- loses at most one batch and the verification block below shows it.
--
-- Totals: 3531 rows · 701 emotions · 42 subjects.

-- rows 1–250
ON CONFLICT (emotion, subject_slug) DO NOTHING;

